.TH ATS-VIEWER 1 2026-10-15 "ats-viewer 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ats-viewer \- show what a recruiter sees after an ATS parses a resume
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ats-viewer
.I resume
.RB [ \-o
.IR report.html ]
.br
.B ats-viewer serve
.RI [ port ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ats-viewer
extracts the text layer of a resume, parses it into the field schema used by
applicant tracking systems, and writes an HTML report of the resulting
candidate profile.
.PP
The schema and post-processing mirror the candidate-side JavaScript of
Workday, Lever and Greenhouse. Their server-side parsers are closed, so the
extracted values are a heuristic estimate, not the vendors' exact output.
.PP
A one-line summary and the most severe findings are printed to standard
output.
.PP
With
.BR serve ,
it runs a local upload page instead (see
.BR "WEB UPLOAD PAGE" ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I resume
Input file. Supported: PDF
.RB ( .pdf ),
Word
.RB ( .docx ),
HTML
.RB ( .html ", " .htm )
and plain text
.RB ( .txt ).
Legacy binary Word
.RB ( .doc )
is not supported; save it as DOCX first.
.IP
DOCX text is read the way Apache Tika orders it: header parts, then the
body, then footer parts. VBA macros, tables, text boxes and header or
footer text are reported as findings.
.TP
.BI \-o " report.html"
Write the report to this path. Default:
.IB name .ats.html
in the current directory, where
.I name
is the input file name without its extension.
.TP
.BI serve " \fR[\fPport\fR]\fP"
Start the upload page on
.BI http://127.0.0.1: port
(default 8080).
.SH WEB UPLOAD PAGE
The server listens on the loopback address only. Choose or drop a resume
(PDF, DOCX, HTML or TXT, up to 20 MB) and the same report is shown in the
browser. Each upload is written to an owner-only temporary file, parsed,
and deleted; nothing is stored or sent elsewhere. Unsupported types return
HTTP 400, unparseable files 422, and files over 20 MB 413.
.SH REPORT
.TP
.B Parse health
Score out of 100 (high finding \-12, medium \-5, low \-1). This is the
tool's own heuristic, not a vendor confidence score. Also lists upload
acceptance: Workday (PDF, DOC, DOCX, HTML, TXT, up to 5 MB), Ashby (up to
6 MB) and Lever (up to 100 MB).
.TP
.B Findings
Missing name, email or phone; DOCX macros, tables, text boxes and
header or footer text; placeholder URLs; non-standard or combined
section headers; page headers and footers in the text layer, including
those merged into job descriptions; words split by stray spaces; jobs
without a title or company; end dates other than
.B Present
(only
.B Present
sets Workday's "I currently work here");
certifications placed under Education; no spoken languages; mixed date
formats.
.TP
.B Character scan
Replacement characters, private-use glyphs, ligatures, control
characters, symbols and fancy bullets, smart quotes, dashes and other
non-ASCII characters, each with sample context.
.TP
.B Workday
Name split into first, middle and last; email; phone with inferred country
code; city, region and country; websites (those without
.B http
are flagged as dropped); work experience; education, with field of study
fuzzy-matched to a reference list (Jaro similarity of at least 0.75,
case-insensitive) and degree matched approximately; certifications;
languages; skills.
.TP
.B Lever
Name, email, phone, current company, location, and links bucketed into
LinkedIn, Twitter, GitHub, Quora and Other. Only the last Other link is kept.
.TP
.B Greenhouse
No parsing at apply time; the recruiter sees typed fields, the file and
its text.
.TP
.B Keyword search
Exact-match search over lowercased text with punctuation replaced by
spaces. No stemming or synonyms.
.TP
.B Raw text
The full extracted text layer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Report written.
.TP
.B 1
Input unreadable, unsupported type, text extraction failed, or report not
writable.
.TP
.B 2
No input file given.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ats-viewer resume.pdf
ats-viewer resume.html \-o /tmp/report.html
ats-viewer serve 3000
.fi
.SH BUGS
Legacy .doc input is not supported. The location split assumes a city of one or
two words, so "Acme San Francisco, CA" is read as company "Acme San".
Section headers in all capitals that are not recognized, such as a company
name like "IBM" on its own line, are treated as unknown sections.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pdftotext (1)
